# Little Browser: in the vertical strip a tab can be dragged between the pinned and the unpinned
# area, live, the way it moves into and out of a tab group. The pointer picks the area (above the
# middle of the "+ New Tab" row is pinned), and entering the other area pins or unpins the dragged
# tabs; split views move whole. A drag that includes a tab group stays among the unpinned tabs,
# since pinned tabs can't be grouped. Upstream rebuilds a tab's view when its pin state changes,
# which would free the views the drag holds, so a dragged tab keeps its view instead. Cancelling
# the drag restores the original pin state; tabs dragged on into another window keep the state they
# have when they leave.
